WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.331
Cover Letter.

2
00:00:01.611 --> 00:00:05.515
Day 81 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Career phase.

3
00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:08.289
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.569 --> 00:00:18.148
Today's goal: write a short cover letter or application email that explains why you, why this role and why this company, in under 250 words.

5
00:00:18.428 --> 00:00:21.095
Many recruiters skim, so be specific and brief.

6
00:00:22.445 --> 00:00:23.298
Part 1.

7
00:00:23.578 --> 00:00:24.751
When do you need one?

8
00:00:26.001 --> 00:00:27.345
Here is a quick table:

9
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:29.503
Situation, and Cover letter?.

10
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:31.425
The application asks for it:

11
00:00:31.705 --> 00:00:32.836
Yes, always.

12
00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:34.460
Applying by email:

13
00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.535
Yes, the email body is your cover letter (shorter).

14
00:00:37.815 --> 00:00:39.137
Career switch or gap:

15
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:41.465
Yes, to explain it positively.

16
00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:43.196
Applying with a referral:

17
00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:46.441
Optional; a short note to the hiring manager helps.

18
00:00:46.721 --> 00:00:48.257
Quick portal easy apply:

19
00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:49.711
Usually optional.

20
00:00:51.061 --> 00:00:51.935
Part 2.

21
00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:53.794
The 4-paragraph structure.

22
00:00:55.044 --> 00:00:55.961
Step 1:

23
00:00:56.241 --> 00:01:00.231
Hook: the role you're applying for, and one line on why you're a strong fit.

24
00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:01.428
Step 2:

25
00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:02.476
Proof:

26
00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:06.617
2 to 3 achievements that match the job description, with numbers.

27
00:01:06.897 --> 00:01:07.815
Step 3:

28
00:01:08.095 --> 00:01:11.807
Why them: something specific about the company, product or team.

29
00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:13.047
Step 4:

30
00:01:13.327 --> 00:01:16.441
Close: thank them, and a clear, confident next step.

31
00:01:17.791 --> 00:01:18.687
Part 3.

32
00:01:18.967 --> 00:01:20.354
Example cover letter.

33
00:01:21.604 --> 00:01:23.481
Here is a template you can copy.

34
00:01:23.761 --> 00:01:24.807
Dear Ms.

35
00:01:25.087 --> 00:01:25.791
Rao.

36
00:01:26.071 --> 00:01:31.063
I'm applying for the Senior Backend Engineer role on your payments platform team (job.

37
00:01:31.343 --> 00:01:33.860
ID 4471).

38
00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:42.204
With nine years of building high-scale payment systems in Java and Kafka, I'm. confident I can. help your team scale reliably.

39
00:01:42.484 --> 00:01:51.551
At XYZ Technologies, I led the re-architecture of our checkout using the outbox. pattern, cutting. failed orders by 60%.

40
00:01:51.831 --> 00:02:03.905
I also reduced payment failures from 3% to 0.5% by adding. retries and a. backup gateway, and I mentored four engineers, two of whom have since been promoted.

41
00:02:04.185 --> 00:02:06.255
The rest of the template is on the page.

42
00:02:09.105 --> 00:02:10.022
Part 4.

43
00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:12.521
Application email (short version).

44
00:02:13.771 --> 00:02:15.648
Here is a template you can copy.

45
00:02:15.928 --> 00:02:16.803
Subject:

46
00:02:17.083 --> 00:02:23.333
Application, Senior Backend Engineer (ID 4471), Ashish Gupta.

47
00:02:23.613 --> 00:02:24.659
Dear Ms.

48
00:02:24.939 --> 00:02:25.643
Rao.

49
00:02:25.923 --> 00:02:28.931
I'd like to apply for the Senior Backend Engineer role.

50
00:02:29.211 --> 00:02:40.560
I have nine years of. experience. building payment systems in Java and Kafka, most recently leading a checkout. re-architecture. that cut failed orders by 60%.

51
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.248
I've attached my resume.

52
00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.536
I'd be glad to discuss how I can help your payments team.

53
00:02:45.816 --> 00:02:46.883
Best regards.

54
00:02:47.163 --> 00:02:49.232
The rest of the template is on the page.

55
00:02:52.082 --> 00:02:53.042
Part 5.

56
00:02:53.322 --> 00:02:54.538
Phrases that help.

57
00:02:55.788 --> 00:02:57.132
Here is a quick table:

58
00:02:57.412 --> 00:02:59.097
Part, and Useful phrases.

59
00:02:59.377 --> 00:03:00.188
Opening:

60
00:03:00.468 --> 00:03:02.025
I'm writing to apply for...

61
00:03:02.305 --> 00:03:04.396
I was excited to see your opening for...

62
00:03:04.676 --> 00:03:06.809
Name suggested I contact you about...

63
00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:07.729
Fit:

64
00:03:08.009 --> 00:03:09.865
With X years of experience in...

65
00:03:10.145 --> 00:03:12.855
My background in... makes me a strong fit for...

66
00:03:13.135 --> 00:03:13.903
Proof:

67
00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:16.721
At company, I led... which resulted in...

68
00:03:17.001 --> 00:03:19.284
I was responsible for... and achieved...

69
00:03:19.564 --> 00:03:20.353
Why them:

70
00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.084
I've followed your work on...

71
00:03:22.364 --> 00:03:24.988
Your focus on... matches my interest in...

72
00:03:25.268 --> 00:03:26.377
Gap or switch:

73
00:03:26.657 --> 00:03:29.836
After a planned career break to care for my family, I...

74
00:03:30.116 --> 00:03:34.127
I'm moving from QA into development, and over the last two years I've...

75
00:03:34.407 --> 00:03:35.217
Close:

76
00:03:35.497 --> 00:03:37.652
I'd welcome the opportunity to discuss...

77
00:03:37.932 --> 00:03:40.279
Thank you for your time and consideration.

78
00:03:41.629 --> 00:03:42.567
Part 6.

79
00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:44.149
Mistakes to avoid.

80
00:03:45.399 --> 00:03:46.252
Avoid:

81
00:03:46.532 --> 00:03:52.591
To whom it may concern (find the hiring manager's name if you can; otherwise Dear Hiring Manager).

82
00:03:52.871 --> 00:03:53.724
Avoid:

83
00:03:54.004 --> 00:03:55.519
Repeating your whole resume.

84
00:03:55.799 --> 00:03:56.652
Avoid:

85
00:03:56.932 --> 00:03:59.876
Generic praise (Your company is a leading company).

86
00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:01.009
Avoid:

87
00:04:01.289 --> 00:04:04.084
Talking only about what you want, not what they need.

88
00:04:04.364 --> 00:04:05.217
Avoid:

89
00:04:05.497 --> 00:04:08.975
Over 1 page, or the wrong company name (check before sending!).

90
00:04:10.325 --> 00:04:11.263
Part 7.

91
00:04:11.543 --> 00:04:14.871
Conversation: asking about the hiring manager's name.

92
00:04:16.121 --> 00:04:18.148
Here is how the conversation goes.

93
00:04:18.428 --> 00:04:23.591
Hi Riya, I'm preparing my application for the Senior Backend Engineer role.

94
00:04:23.871 --> 00:04:26.516
Could I ask who the hiring manager is?

95
00:04:26.796 --> 00:04:30.188
Sure, it's Kavita Rao, the engineering manager for payments.

96
00:04:30.468 --> 00:04:31.407
Thank you.

97
00:04:31.687 --> 00:04:34.844
Should I send a cover letter, or is the resume enough?

98
00:04:35.124 --> 00:04:37.279
A short cover letter helps for this team.

99
00:04:37.559 --> 00:04:39.009
Keep it to one page.

100
00:04:39.289 --> 00:04:40.185
Got it.

101
00:04:40.465 --> 00:04:43.388
Is there anything specific the team is looking for?

102
00:04:44.738 --> 00:04:46.338
The conversation continues.

103
00:04:46.618 --> 00:04:50.543
Experience with high-volume payment systems, and strong communication.

104
00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.253
That's very helpful.

105
00:04:52.533 --> 00:04:55.263
I'll send everything by tomorrow morning.

106
00:04:55.543 --> 00:04:57.058
Perfect, thanks Ashish.

107
00:04:58.408 --> 00:04:59.283
Part 8.

108
00:04:59.563 --> 00:05:00.480
Practice.

109
00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.970
Write the Proof paragraph for a role you want:

110
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:07.663
2 achievements with numbers that match the job description.

111
00:05:09.013 --> 00:05:09.909
Part 9.

112
00:05:10.189 --> 00:05:11.235
Speak today.

113
00:05:12.485 --> 00:05:16.090
Draft a 4-paragraph cover letter for one real job posting.

114
00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.933
Write a 4-line application email using the short version.

115
00:05:20.213 --> 00:05:21.301
Read it aloud.

116
00:05:21.581 --> 00:05:23.885
If you run out of breath in a sentence, split it.

117
00:05:25.235 --> 00:05:26.771
That's the end of this lesson.

118
00:05:27.051 --> 00:05:31.701
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

119
00:05:31.981 --> 00:05:38.104
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

